      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Think of cholesterol like fat in your blood, which needs to be transported throughout your body. LDL is often called \"bad\" cholesterol because high levels can build up in your arteries, leading to blockages. Conversely, HDL is considered \"good\" cholesterol because it helps carry excess cholesterol away from your arteries and back to the liver for removal, protecting your heart.",
